cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "rPPG-PTSD: contactless heart rate and HRV measurement module for PTSD-relevant physiological research"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "kaiyneee"
repository-code: "https://github.com/kaiyneee/rppg-Pulse-detection-from-video"
abstract: >
  A modular remote-photoplethysmography (rPPG) pipeline (MediaPipe Face
  Landmarker + 6 signal-extraction methods + SQI-gated quality control +
  HRV feature extraction) for contactless measurement of heart rate and
  heart-rate-variability markers potentially relevant to PTSD research.
  Not a diagnostic or screening tool — see README.md.
references:
  - type: conference-paper
    title: "Detecting Pulse from Head Motions in Video"
    authors:
      - family-names: Balakrishnan
        given-names: Guha
      - family-names: Durand
        given-names: Fredo
      - family-names: Guttag
        given-names: John
    year: 2013
    collection-title: "IEEE Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR)"
    notes: "Head-motion (ballistocardiographic) extraction method; original scientific inspiration for this project."
  - type: article
    title: "Robust Pulse Rate From Chrominance-Based rPPG"
    authors:
      - family-names: de Haan
        given-names: Gerard
      - family-names: Jeanne
        given-names: Vincent
    year: 2013
    journal: "IEEE Transactions on Biomedical Engineering"
    notes: "CHROM color-based extraction method."
  - type: article
    title: "Algorithmic Principles of Remote PPG"
    authors:
      - family-names: Wang
        given-names: Wenjin
      - family-names: den Brinker
        given-names: Albertus C.
      - family-names: Stuijk
        given-names: Sander
      - family-names: de Haan
        given-names: Gerard
    year: 2016
    journal: "IEEE Transactions on Biomedical Engineering"
    notes: "POS color-based extraction method (default)."
  - type: article
    title: "Non-contact, automated cardiac pulse measurements using video imaging and blind source separation"
    authors:
      - family-names: Poh
        given-names: Ming-Zher
      - family-names: McDuff
        given-names: Daniel J.
      - family-names: Picard
        given-names: Rosalind W.
    year: 2010
    journal: "Optics Express"
    notes: "ICA color-based extraction method."
  - type: conference-paper
    title: "Measuring pulse rate with a webcam - a non-contact method for evaluating cardiac activity"
    authors:
      - family-names: Lewandowska
        given-names: Magdalena
      - family-names: Ruminski
        given-names: Jacek
      - family-names: Kowalik
        given-names: Tomasz
      - family-names: Nowak
        given-names: Jedrzej
    year: 2011
    collection-title: "Federated Conference on Computer Science and Information Systems (FedCSIS)"
    notes: "PCA color-based extraction method."
  - type: article
    title: "Remote plethysmographic imaging using ambient light"
    authors:
      - family-names: Verkruysse
        given-names: Wim
      - family-names: Svaasand
        given-names: Lars O.
      - family-names: Nelson
        given-names: J. Stuart
    year: 2008
    journal: "Optics Express"
    notes: "GREEN-channel extraction method."
  - type: article
    title: "An advanced detrending method with application to HRV analysis"
    authors:
      - family-names: Tarvainen
        given-names: Mika P.
      - family-names: Ranta-aho
        given-names: Perttu O.
      - family-names: Karjalainen
        given-names: Pasi A.
    year: 2002
    journal: "IEEE Transactions on Biomedical Engineering"
    notes: "Smoothness-priors detrending; lambda recalibrated for 30 fps in this project, see scripts/analyze_tarvainen_lambda.py."
  - type: software
    title: "head-pulse-track"
    authors:
      - name: "irfan798"
    repository-code: "https://github.com/irfan798/head-pulse-track"
    notes: >
      Scientific inspiration that first pointed at Balakrishnan et al. (2013)
      for this problem. That repository carries no license (all rights
      reserved by its authors); no source code from it is reused in this
      project, which is an independent implementation built on the
      MediaPipe Face Landmarker Tasks API. See README.md "Acknowledgements".
